 "notes": [
  {
   "text": "US stocks rallied on Wednesday, Nov 11, 2026, with the S&P 500 up about 1.5% at midday and the Nasdaq 100 up 2.8%, after CoreWeave reported third-quarter revenue up 168% to $3.7 billion and raised full-year guidance to $13.0-13.3 billion, above the $12.86 billion analysts expected; its shares rose about 21% and Nvidia gained 3.15% in early trading after a two-day slide that erased more than $430 billion of market value.",
   "source": "TheStreet",
   "url": "https://www.thestreet.com/stock-market-today/stock-market-today-dow-jones-sp-500-nasdaq-updates-nov-11-2026"
  },
  {
   "text": "No scheduled federal economic release landed on Nov 11, 2026 (Veterans Day, with the bond market closed); the private CNBC/NRF Retail Monitor put October total retail sales at $561.7 billion, up 0.2% on the month and 3.6% on the year, the smallest monthly gain since November 2025, with no published consensus.",
   "source": "TheStreet",
   "url": "https://www.thestreet.com/stock-market-today/stock-market-today-dow-jones-sp-500-nasdaq-updates-nov-11-2026"
  },
  {
   "text": "October CPI, released Nov 10, 2026, rose 0.4% on the month against 0.3% expected, with core up 0.3% against 0.2% expected; traders moved to price an 84% chance of a 25 basis point Federal Reserve hike in December and a 15% chance of 50 basis points, the 10-year Treasury yield rose to 4.93%, and the S&P 500 closed down 0.38% with the Nasdaq Composite down 0.74% and Nvidia down 5.47% at $168.89.",
   "source": "Yahoo Finance",
   "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-tuesday-november-10-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-inflation-data-cpi-090627830.html"
  },
  {
   "text": "The October employment report released Nov 6, 2026 put the US unemployment rate at 4.1%, down from 4.2% in September, according to the Federal Reserve Economic Data series UNRATE, which was updated Nov 6 and lists Dec 4, 2026 as the next release.",
   "source": "FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis",
   "url": "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/UNRATE"
  },
  {
   "text": "Scheduled US releases ahead: October PPI on Fri Nov 13, 2026 at 8:30 AM per the Bureau of Labor Statistics schedule, advance October retail sales on Tue Nov 17, FOMC minutes from the Oct 27-28 meeting on Wed Nov 18 at 2:00 PM ET, and the Q3 GDP second estimate with October PCE inflation on Wed Nov 25.",
   "source": "Bureau of Labor Statistics",
   "url": "https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/ppi.htm"
  }
 ]
